    "section": "2.3",
    "heading": "Create Your Character",
    "lineStart": 875,
    "lineEnd": 883
  },
  "section": "2.3",
  "rulesText": "Here are the steps to make a character; each step is explored in detail:\n\n1: Choose a Class. Every adventurer is a member of a class. A class broadly describes a character's vocation, special talents, and favored tactics.\n2: Determine Origin. A character's origin includes two elements: background and species. How did the character spend the years leading up to a life of adventure? Who are the character's ancestors? You can also choose your character's languages.\n3: Determine Ability Scores. Much of what your character does in the game depends on the character's six abilities.\n4: Choose an Alignment. Alignment is a shorthand for your character's moral compass.\n5: Fill in Details. Using the choices you've made, fill in the remaining details on your character sheet."
}
